  "details": "The new TrackingDataType.Origin should give us the origin of the playspace, which works fine, unless the player enters a station. Then we just get a position reported which has nothing to do with the playspace origin anymore. \nWe expect that the distance and offset between origin and head tracking data does not change when entering a station, since it shouldn't be related to that. \nNote: VRChat already sets the origin y to be at ground level, which is already an unexpected behaviour. The offset change when entering a station however is even more unexpected. We need to work out the relative positions from tracking data in the users playspace to get rid of feedback loops that we experience with IK and humanoid bone positions from a player, especially in a station, so a consistent behaviour here is important for us.\nNote: This was tested with a custom laying animation. The reported original was suddenly a few centimeters below the head tracking data when being in the station, but fine when not being in the station.",
